<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Islamic Emirate of Afghanistan (2021-present)</h1><p class="st-meta">2021 CE – present · capital Kabul</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The restored Taliban state, which took Kabul in August 2021 and has imposed sweeping restrictions on women while seeking international recognition.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After a twenty-year insurgency against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/islamic-republic-of-afghanistan">Islamic Republic of Afghanistan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a> forces, and the US withdrawal agreed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/doha">Doha</a> in 2020, the Taliban seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a> on 15 August 2021 and restored the Islamic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hibatullah-akhundzada">Hibatullah Akhundzada</a>, the movement's leader since 2016, became supreme leader.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The supreme leader rules from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kandahar">Kandahar</a> by decree, with a caretaker cabinet in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a> and no constitution or elections. The regime has banned girls from secondary and higher education and restricted women's work, travel and public life. Foreign aid cuts and frozen assets caused economic collapse and humanitarian crisis, though security improved in many areas. It faces an insurgency by the Islamic State <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khorasan">Khorasan</a> Province.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>The Islamic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> remains in power. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> became the first state to formally recognise it in 2025, while most countries engage with it without recognition.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/islamic-emirate-of-afghanistan-2021-present.jpg" alt="Islamic Emirate of Afghanistan (2021-present)" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Original: Taliban Vector: Lexicon · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Taliban.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>2021 CE – present</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kabul</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Hibatullah Akhundzada</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam (Deobandi)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Pashto, Dari</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Afghanistan, Taliban Afghanistan</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=2024&amp;focus=islamic-emirate-of-afghanistan-2021-present" aria-label="Islamic Emirate of Afghanistan (2021-present) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6437 927 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Islamic Emirate of Afghanistan (2021-present) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6757 1183L6757 1183M6757 1183L6690 1235"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6757 1183h0M6690 1235h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6757 1183h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6757 1183h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kabul. <a href="/atlas?year=2024&amp;focus=islamic-emirate-of-afghanistan-2021-present">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
